DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260606
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
X-MICROSOFT-MSNCALENDAR-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
SUMMARY:AMC150 Worcester Chapter TrailsFest: 20s & 30s East-West Trail Hik
 e - Prospect Hill and Newton Hill
LOCATION:126 Salisbury St #10\nWorcester\, MA
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 6\, 2026 | 8:30 AM\nhttps://activities.outdoor
 s.org/s/oc-activity/a5UVX0000016iFV2AY/\nJoin the Worcester Chapter 20s & 
 30s on a ~4 mile hike along a segment of the East-West Trail\, which trave
 rses the city of Worcester over 14 miles. This hike will take us through 
 Institute Park\, Salisbury Park\, and Elm Park over a variety of terrain -
 - from the trails up to Newton Hill to walking through neighborhoods near 
 Prospect Hill. One notable landmark on the hike is Bancroft Tower\, a 125-
 year-old 56-foot-high (17 m) tower of granite and natural stone. We will p
 lan on ending our hike at Bancroft Tower and spending some time there. Des
 pite the short mileage\, there is an expected elevation gain of around 630
  ft throughout the hike centered around Prospect Hill and Newton Hill.Part
 icipants must bring:Minimum 1 liter of waterSnacks as necessaryLayers as t
 he weather dictates\, including outer shellHiking shoes or boots with good
  treadBackpack to carry gearConfirmed participants can expect an email a f
 ew days before the activity with weather\, meeting location\, and parking 
 details.After this trip\, please join us for the AMC150 Worcester Chapter 
 TrailsFest 2026\, taking place Saturday\, June 6\, 2026 at Institute Park 
 in Worcester! TrailsFest\, which has been held annually since 2018\, coinc
 ides with National Trails Day and is co-hosted by a group of organizations
  including the Appalachian Mountain Club and Park Spirit.At this event\, w
 e celebrate trails in all their forms\, including hiking trails\, bike pat
 hs\, waterways\, and climbing routes. Here is what the day will look like:
 Morning through 12pm: Activities like this one throughout the area.12pm to
  4:00pm: AMC150 Worcester Chapter TrailsFest celebration at Institute Park
 . Food\, live music\, speakers\, friends\, and fun!BYO non-alcoholic bever
 ages and a chair.Bring yourself\, your friends and family\, and spread the
  word!In 2026\, the Appalachian Mountain Club is celebrating 150 years of 
 protecting\, enjoying\, and understanding the outdoors! At the heart of th
 e celebration is the AMC 150th Outdoor Relay—a connected series of outdo
 or adventures traveling from Virginia to Maine with a commemorative AMC fl
 ag carried along the entire route.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a5UVX00000178pt2AA
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260510T025151Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260606
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
X-MICROSOFT-MSNCALENDAR-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
SUMMARY:AMC150 Worcester Chapter TrailsFest: 20s & 30s East-West Trail Hik
 e - Boynton Park to Institute Park
LOCATION:Institute Park\, 126 Salisbury St\nWorcester\, MA
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 6\, 2026 | 6:30 AM\nhttps://activities.outdoor
 s.org/s/oc-activity/a5UVX00000178pt2AA/\nLooking for a challenge on the mo
 rning of Trailsfest? Join the 20s & 30s group for a hike that will cover m
 ore than half of the entire Worcester East-West Trail! We will be hiking a
  9 mile section of this trail that will include 14 out of the 22 Green Spa
 ces that the East-West Trail features. This route will include urban secti
 ons as well as we cut across the City of Worcester to make our way to all 
 of these stops. The elevation gain for this hike will be ~750ft\, includin
 g ~1200ft of descent.We will be carspotting for this hike. We will meet at
  Institute Park and drive over to Boynton Park to start our hike. We likel
 y will ask for at least three participants to help with driving. All parti
 ciants will be required to fill out a screening form before being confirme
 d for this hike. This form will also include a list of eqiupment/items tha
 t will be required for this hike. Heavy rain or thunderstorms will cancel 
 this hike\, and the leaders will be in communication as time gets closer i
 f inclement weather seems likely. After this trip\, please join us for the
  AMC150 Worcester Chapter TrailsFest 2026\, taking place Saturday\, June
  6\, 2026 at Institute Park in Worcester! TrailsFest\, which has been held
  annually since 2018\, coincides with National Trails Day and is co-hosted
  by a group of organizations including the Appalachian Mountain Club and P
 ark Spirit.At this event\, we celebrate trails in all their forms\, includ
 ing hiking trails\, bike paths\, waterways\, and climbing routes. Here is 
 what the day will look like:Morning through 12pm: Activities like this one
  throughout the area.12pm to 4:00pm: AMC150 Worcester Chapter TrailsFest c
 elebration at Institute Park. Food\, live music\, speakers\, friends\, and
  fun!BYO non-alcoholic beverages and a chair.Bring yourself\, your friends
  and family\, and spread the word!In 2026\, the Appalachian Mountain Club 
 is celebrating 150 years of protecting\, enjoying\, and understanding the 
 outdoors! At the heart of the celebration is the AMC 150th Outdoor Relay
 —a connected series of outdoor adventures traveling from Virginia to Mai
 ne with a commemorative AMC flag carried along the entire route.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a5UVX00000152yH2AQ
